{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["And the reason for <b>For every man whoever curses his father and his mother</b>: it refers back to the beginning of the passage, which stated, \"Every man: his mother and his father you shall fear\" (Leviticus 19:3), and it states here, \"For every man whoever will not hearken to Me and will curse his father and his mother, he shall surely be put to death.\"\n\nAnd by way of truth: because it stated (Leviticus 20:7), \"And you shall sanctify yourselves and you shall be holy, for I am YHWH your Elohim,\" and it stated (Leviticus 20:8), \"I am YHWH who sanctifies you\" — for the glorious Name, He it is that sanctifies us, for He is our Father and our Redeemer from of old is His name — if so, one who curses those who are partners in formation is liable to death. And this is the reason for the law of the male and female adulterers, which it placed adjacent here and set before all the forbidden relations, and I have already hinted at this above (Exodus 20:13).\n\nNow Scripture mentioned some of the forbidden relations to subject them to the death penalty, and they are: another man's wife, a father's wife, the daughter-in-law, a male with a male, and a woman with her mother (Leviticus 20:10–14) — and the same applies to a woman with her daughter and her daughter's daughter, for it mentioned some of a woman's relatives, and the same applies to all those mentioned there (Leviticus 18:17) in the warning, and all the more so her own relatives, his son's daughter and his daughter's daughter, who are mentioned (Leviticus 18:10) — and needless to say, his own daughter. And in all this there are further midrashic derivations to make them liable.\n\nLikewise it mentioned the liability for bestiality to the death penalty (Leviticus 20:15–16), and then repeated another karet for the menstruant (Leviticus 20:18), to make him liable for mere contact (העראה) without completion of intercourse — this is what it says, \"her flow he uncovered\" (Leviticus 20:18) — and likewise for a maternal aunt and a paternal aunt: \"for he uncovered his relative\" (Leviticus 20:19). And it mentioned one's aunt and likewise a brother's wife (Leviticus 20:20–21), to make them liable for the punishment of excision, whether the brother had children or did not. And the karet stated regarding one's sister (Leviticus 20:17) is superfluous, and is expounded by our Sages (Makkot 14a): \"Why did karet for one's sister come out…\" etc.\n\nAnd by way of the plain sense, it adds in the karet \"before the eyes of the children of their people\" (Leviticus 20:17), to say that their soul will die in youth, in the sense that they will see and understand and consider together that the hand of YHWH has done this, and the Holy One of Israel has decreed it. And the reason for \"he shall bear his iniquity\" is that that sin will cleave to him from that time onward — his deeds will not prosper and the curse will lie upon him, for HaShem will strike him with evil diseases until His destruction of him in karet, as in the matter they stated (Shabbat 33a): a sign of transgression is the spreading eruption. And there was no need to mention the other karet-liabilities, such as one's mother (Leviticus 18:7) and a wife's sister (Leviticus 18:18), for we have already learned from those mentioned all that is necessary."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:57:05.835594110Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}